Q: Mockito is currently self-attaching to enable the inline-mock-maker. This will no longer work in future releases of the JDK A: <p>I had same issue, Adding @<strong>SpringBootTest</strong> annotation to test class fixes for me,</p>
<p>I am using JDK 23 and SpringBoot 4.01</p>
<p>here is my example code</p>
<pre><code>@SpringBootTest
public class ProductServiceTests {

    @MockitoBean
    private ProductRepository productRepository;

    @Autowired
    private ProductService productService;

    Optional&lt;Product&gt; prod1 = Optional.of(Product.builder().id(&quot;1&quot;).name(&quot;name1&quot;).build());

    @Test
    public void findByIdReturnsProduct() {
        String id = &quot;1&quot;;
        Mockito.when(productRepository.findById(any(String.class))).thenReturn(prod1);

        Mono&lt;Product&gt; result = productService.findById(id);

        StepVerifier.create(result)
                .expectNext(prod1.get())
                .verifyComplete();
    }
}
</code></pre>
